## Provenance

- The pack machinery (`helpers/packs.py`) and the transport engine
  (`helpers/sync.py`) are ports of the Khan fork's `helpers/device_sync.py`
  and `helpers/continuity_sync.py`
  (https://github.com/duketopceo/khan), itself MIT-licensed work by
  Luke Kimball / duketopceo.
- Khan's memory packs rode `horde.memory.MemoryAtomStore`; this plugin
  replaces that coupling with a pluggable `MemoryBackend` protocol plus a
  MemFS-style `git` backend (atom store = a git repo of JSON files).
- Peer endpoints moved under `/api/plugins/device_sync/*` and peer auth is
  a shared bearer token instead of session auth — machine-to-machine sync
  can't ride browser credentials.

